<title>Falling for Games auction (Chicagoland pickup/USA shipping)--ENDS TOMORROW</title>
<description>It's autumn, and as the leaves fall I'm reminded 1) that I don't want any games to fall off my shelf, and 2) you just might fall in love with the games I have. Why not offer an auction to satisfy 1 and 2?

Here are the rules for the auction:

1. All bids must be in whole dollars, starting with the minimum bid. [b]Bids below the minimum bid will not be considered.[/b] It would be great if you could include your ZIP in your bid (or if you will be doing local pickup) so I know how to estimate costs once the auction ends.

2. You may pick up your games locally in Chicago's west suburbs (near Lombard or Carol Stream).

3. Shipping is from 60148 if you'd like to estimate beforehand and will be paid by the item's winner. I will ship via USPS or UPS (whichever is cheaper), and I'll try to keep costs as low as I can (I use PirateShip and should have plenty of large boxes). Shipping is offered to USA addresses only.

4. All shipping transactions will be conducted via Zelle, Venmo, or PayPal. If you are doing local pickup, I require cash. All sales will go through the marketplace to ensure that BGG gets its 3% cut.

5. I reserve the right to remove items from this list that have no bids. I may also add items to the auction in progress.

6. This particular auction will run until sometime in the afternoon on [b]Saturday, November 8[/b].

7. If you have any questions, please ask. (Geekmail preferred.)

Happy bidding!</description>

